1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,440
In 2019, a typical New Brunswick home cost about $172,000.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,689
Today? About $352,000.

3
00:00:10,834 --> 00:00:12,870
It doubled. So, why?

4
00:00:17,243 --> 00:00:19,183
Reason 1: more people.

5
00:00:19,243 --> 00:00:25,043
During the pandemic, buyers from Ontario and beyond discovered New Brunswick was a bargain.

6
00:00:25,103 --> 00:00:31,556
Then came record immigration. The province grew by about 25,000 people in a single year.

7
00:00:32,243 --> 00:00:34,283
Reason 2: not enough homes.

8
00:00:34,343 --> 00:00:37,683
The province says it needs 6,000 new homes a year.

9
00:00:37,743 --> 00:00:42,566
In 2022, builders started about 4,680.

10
00:00:42,957 --> 00:00:45,497
Reason 3: building got expensive.

11
00:00:45,557 --> 00:00:50,815
Lumber, labour and borrowing all cost more, so every new home costs more to build.

12
00:00:51,529 --> 00:00:54,719
More people. Too few homes. Higher costs.

13
00:00:54,779 --> 00:00:58,791
And when demand outruns supply, prices only go one way.

14
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:03,281
So, New Brunswick: how do we build faster?
